This assert statement checks if the return value of `LastIndexOf` is non-negative, then it checks if `x` appeared in the array list. Otherwise, it checks if `x` is not in its current location.--------------------
Debug.Assert(New_Ret >= 0 && arrList.Contains(x));
</code>

Please note, in C# `&&` is a logical operator AND, it returns true if both conditions are true, otherwise it returns false. `arrList.Contains(x)` guarantees that if the returned value is non-negative, x is definitely there in arrList.--------------------
Debug.Assert(New_Ret >= 0 || !Old_arrListContainsX);
